  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/can1357/oh-my-pi/zipball/v18.22.0",
  "body": "## @oh-my-pi/pi-ai\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed slow streaming of Gemma tool calls with large arguments.\n\n## @oh-my-pi/pi-coding-agent\n\n### Breaking Changes\n\n- Moved binary analysis from the standalone `ida` and `ghidra` tools into the backend-neutral `dsm` namespace (`xd://eval/dsm`).\n- Replaced the `ida.enabled`, `ida.maxOpen`, and `ida.idleCloseSec` settings with `disassembler.backend`, `disassembler.maxOpen`, and `disassembler.idleCloseSec`; shared disassembler database APIs are now available under `@oh-my-pi/pi-coding-agent/disasm`.\n\n### Added\n\n- Added Tern plan review editing and comments: double-click plans to edit them, select text to add Google Docs-style comments, and send comments to Refine.\n- Added Ghidra support with automatic setup of Ghidra, JDK, and PyGhidra when analysis is explicitly requested; Auto mode uses an installed IDA Pro when available and otherwise falls back to Ghidra.\n- Added support for sharing live analysis databases with child agents through `db.handle()` and `dsm.open(handle)`.\n- Added a `Force Remove` option to `worktree.onExit` that removes session-created worktrees without prompting, including worktrees with uncommitted changes; new commits remain on the worktree branch.\n\n### Changed\n\n- Updated Tern plan review with a single Approve control, comment-aware Refine option, model selection, and a Save action that writes the plan while keeping review open and plan mode active.\n- Plain executable reads now display Mach-O, ELF, and PE metadata without opening an analysis database or downloading a backend; request an overview, function details, or `dsm.open()` to begin analysis.\n- Improved the model switcher (`Alt+P` / `/switch`) with provider filtering and per-switch thinking-level selection. In Tern, it now opens above the composer with integrated search, provider and Task/Main filters, and a thinking-level slider.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Deleting or moving large directory trees inside a project no longer stalls language-server file watching ([#19490](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/pull/19490) by [@H4vC](https://github.com/H4vC)).\n- Reduced CPU and memory usage for long-running subagents as their sessions grow ([#19486](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/pull/19486) by [@H4vC](https://github.com/H4vC)).\n- Fixed `commit.draft()` incorrectly classifying files deleted or renamed through bash or eval as “Not yours”; they now appear under Review.\n\n### Removed\n\n- Removed the legacy standalone disassembler tools and their associated prompt instructions.\n- Removed the Copy and Edit-in-editor buttons from the Tern plan review sheet; use selection copying and double-click editing instead.\n\n## @oh-my-pi/collab-web\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Improved streaming performance in the collab viewer, preventing long replies from becoming progressively slower as they are received.\n\n## @oh-my-pi/pi-natives\n\n### Breaking Changes\n\n- `TtyWriter` now requires a drain threshold and callback and only supports independently reopenable TTYs. Its pending UTF-8 byte bounds are reported conservatively.\n\n### Changed\n\n- Large terminal repaints are handled more efficiently, reducing JavaScript-thread work and releasing oversized buffers after output drains.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed stalled terminal writers continuing to emit output or leaking file descriptors after shutdown.\n- Fixed terminal output preserving Unicode across chunk boundaries and safely replacing malformed surrogate sequences.\n\n## @oh-my-pi/pi-tui\n\n### Breaking Changes\n\n- Terminals that support output backpressure must now implement onOutputDrain(callback), which returns an unsubscribe function; terminals without backpressure can omit both pendingOutputBytes and onOutputDrain.\n- Updated PlanReviewOverlay options to use PlanReviewOverlayChoice objects and report choice IDs to onPick and selectOption. Refine and Save actions now reflect plan feedback and saving behavior; removed disabledIndices and externalEditorName, and updated describe to receive DescribeContext.\n\n### Added\n\n- Added configurable model search placement, provider scopes, and an optional thinking-level slider to ModelPickerComponent; selected thinking levels are reported through onPick metadata. The native picker sheet now supports anchoring, scope styling, level display, and icon actions.\n- Added a native plan review document and dock with editable and commentable plans, quote annotations, plan-edit notifications, Approve, Save, and Cancel actions, plus model selection.\n\n### Changed\n\n- Provider scopes now show only the selected provider's models when a provider is chosen, with scope cycling able to return to the full model list.\n- Updated thinking-level controls to use left and right arrow keys, and refreshed the slider and footer hint presentation.\n- Retitled the plan-saving overlay to “Save plan” and updated its action label.\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed slow scrolling and typing in long agent transcripts.\n- Fixed slow typing and cursor movement in drafts longer than 256 lines.\n\n## @oh-my-pi/pi-wire\n\n### Added\n\n- Added optional picker icons for tooltips and accessible names, plus an option to control the placement of the search interface.\n- Added buttons, menu, and document component kinds, including menu-row action state changes and document text editing, commenting, and uncommenting events.\n\n\n## What's Changed\n* perf(coding-agent): stop copying the full message list and journal per publisher flush by @H4vC in https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/pull/19486\n* perf(tui): stop editor wrap-cache thrash and full visual-line rebuilds by @H4vC in https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/pull/19488\n* perf(ai): scan Gemma in-band tool calls incrementally by @H4vC in https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/pull/19487\n* perf(coding-agent): forget vanished directories in the LSP file watcher without full scans by @H4vC in https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/pull/19490\n* perf(collab-web): keep finished Markdown blocks' DOM while streaming by @H4vC in https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/pull/19485\n* perf(tui): reuse the agent transcript viewer's rows between paints by @H4vC in https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/pull/19489\n\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/compare/v18.21.0...v18.22.0",
